=======================

This is /rom: files kept in the paged ROM, read only, there with no card in the
machine.  It's a HydraFS volume, as a card's is, in the paged ROM's banks after
the modules (the disk x: mount '#f' /rom x).

  README          this
  lib/namespace   the default namespace: what's bound and mounted where.
                  init runs it as it starts, and a card's /lib/namespace
                  after it
  lib/profile     what each shell runs as it starts (and a card's
                  /lib/profile after it)
  lib/forth       HyForth's libraries (REQUIRE finds them): its word sets,
                  pre-compiled (REQUIRE tools.fl): coreext.fl, exception.fl,
                  file.fl, facility.fl, string.fl, search.fl, tools.fl,
                  double.fl, and hydra.fl (the sys- words, SH, RUN, banks);
                  hydra.fs, the system's constants and error codes; and
                  startup.fs, what forth loads as it starts
  lib/hylang      hylang's library (load finds a bare name there):
                  danlang's, globals.hl (in hylang as it starts, from its
                  snapshot in the paged ROM), dice.hl and screen.hl
  doc/api.md      the system calls, their registers and their errors
  bin             programs read into RAM to run: mkfs, fsck, label, and
                  grep and sort (in C); scom, a song (an rc script); bound
                  at /bin after the RAM disks'
  songs           songs for play: ZSM files, the Commander X16's (play
                  /rom/songs/test.zsm)
  sample          the SDKs' samples: hi, upper and tick in assembly; in
                  sample/c, hello, upper, code, keys, tones, jukebox and
                  ctest in C

The modules in the paged ROM (the drivers, init, the programs) are under
/dev/mod (#m), a file each.  Cards are under /sd (/sd/0 ... /sd/f), the RAM
disks at /ram (each shell's own area) and /sram (shared).
